{"name":"Arrowhead White","hex":"#f9eaeb","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arrowhead","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The pointed part of an arrow (the weapon).","The pointed part of an arrow (the symbol)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrowhead"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arrowhead","blocks":[{"text":"An arrowhead or point is the usually sharpened and hardened tip of an arrow, which contributes a majority of the projectile mass and is responsible for impacting and penetrating a target, or sometimes for special purposes such as signaling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Fleche_Cartailhac_MHNT_PRE_2009.0.232.2_simple.jpg/330px-Fleche_Cartailhac_MHNT_PRE_2009.0.232.2_simple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrowhead","wikidata":"Q1643900"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=